WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.289
On Christmas morning, the March sisters awoke early because they wanted to surprise Mother with their gifts.

2
00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:13.189
Jo reached under the bed and pulled out a wooden box where the gifts for Mother were hidden.

3
00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:16.535
"I hope Mother likes this," said Jo.

4
00:00:16.536 --> 00:00:19.671
She held up a wrapped parcel close to her heart.

5
00:00:19.672 --> 00:00:22.649
Jo had penned a poem just for Mother.

6
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:27.273
Beth fingered her gift to Mother: two handkerchiefs with daisies.

7
00:00:27.274 --> 00:00:29.688
She had spent all night making them.

8
00:00:29.689 --> 00:00:36.306
Although some of the daisies looked like uneven yellow spots, Beth hoped Mother would love them.

9
00:00:36.307 --> 00:00:42.643
"Smell how lovely that is." Amy pressed a small box under Meg's nose.

10
00:00:42.644 --> 00:00:47.949
"Did you get lavender? It's Mother's favorite," Meg said knowingly.

11
00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:52.591
Amy had used her savings to buy a bottle of cologne for Mother.

12
00:00:52.592 --> 00:00:58.700
"Of course it's lavender, though my personal preference is roses," said Amy.

13
00:00:58.701 --> 00:01:03.871
"Meg, where is your gift?" Jo lifted the wooden box and shook it hard.

14
00:01:03.872 --> 00:01:11.138
"Oh, I have it here," said Meg. From her pocket she pulled out a bundle wrapped in a silk handkerchief.

15
00:01:11.139 --> 00:01:15.036
Inside was a pair of white silk gloves.

16
00:01:15.037 --> 00:01:23.639
Jo squeezed Meg's hand. She knew that Meg had saved her hard earned money to purchase those special gloves.

17
00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:30.277
"They will fit Mother's hands perfectly," Meg said as she lovingly placed them inside the box.

18
00:01:30.278 --> 00:01:34.561
The girls crept quietly downstairs to the living room.

19
00:01:34.562 --> 00:01:40.227
Mother usually reclined in her chair sipping her coffee before the girls scurried in for breakfast.

20
00:01:40.228 --> 00:01:51.253
So, in order to surprise her, the girls tiptoed across the hall and stood quietly outside the living room entrance. Amy had a fit of giggles.

21
00:01:51.254 --> 00:01:54.379
"Shh!" Jo hissed at her.

22
00:01:54.380 --> 00:02:01.629
"Girls, on the count of three," Meg whispered. "One, two . . . THREE!"

23
00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:08.395
The girls flew into the room and shouted simultaneously: "Surprise, Mother! Merry&#8212;!"

24
00:02:08.396 --> 00:02:14.616
But before they could finish their greeting, the girls noticed Mother's chair was unoccupied.

25
00:02:14.617 --> 00:02:19.211
Instead Hannah had just strolled in with a tray full of cakes.

26
00:02:19.212 --> 00:02:24.023
"Ah!" Hannah screamed as she almost flipped the tray over.

27
00:02:24.024 --> 00:02:28.412
Meg ran over to help their beloved housekeeper.

28
00:02:28.413 --> 00:02:35.537
"Oh, girls!" Amy clasped her hands, her eyes growing big as she looked at the dining room table.

29
00:02:35.538 --> 00:02:38.784
The table was covered with heaps of food.

30
00:02:38.785 --> 00:02:46.238
There were sausages, eggs, fresh juice and butter, and cakes adorned each corner.

31
00:02:46.239 --> 00:02:55.700
"Your Ma wanted to surprise you girls with a Christmas feast," said Hannah, still clutching her chest and breathing deeply.

32
00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:59.584
The girls were so touched by their mother's loving act.

33
00:02:59.585 --> 00:03:02.341
"But where is she?" asked Jo.

34
00:03:02.342 --> 00:03:06.990
Before Hannah could answer, Mother walked in through the front door.

35
00:03:06.991 --> 00:03:14.952
"Good morning, my darling girls!" Mother opened her arms wide to embrace her daughters.

36
00:03:14.953 --> 00:03:18.117
"Where did you go, Mother?" Meg asked.

37
00:03:18.118 --> 00:03:21.416
"I went to see the Hummels," replied Mother.

38
00:03:21.417 --> 00:03:25.558
The Hummels were a very poor family with many small children.

39
00:03:25.559 --> 00:03:32.986
Mr. Hummel had been drafted into the army, leaving his pregnant wife and six small children to fend for themselves.

40
00:03:32.987 --> 00:03:40.917
Since Mother worked as a volunteer to help unfortunate people in the community, she knew the Hummels' situation very well.

41
00:03:40.918 --> 00:03:44.520
"How are the children?" asked Beth gently.

42
00:03:44.521 --> 00:03:48.785
"Not very good, I'm afraid," Mother answered gravely.

43
00:03:48.786 --> 00:03:55.888
"They have no heating or . . . food." Her voice trailed off as she looked at the feast on the table.

44
00:03:55.889 --> 00:04:03.280
The girls knew what Mother was thinking, but except for Beth, the other girls were reluctant to part with their Christmas meal.

45
00:04:03.281 --> 00:04:07.512
Meg reasoned to herself: "We don't get any gifts.

46
00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:10.948
We should at least get a decent Christmas meal."

47
00:04:10.949 --> 00:04:17.652
Jo was thinking: "I'm starving! And those sausages look so appetizing!"

48
00:04:17.653 --> 00:04:24.684
Amy contemplated: "Maybe we can eat first then give the rest away to the Hummels."

49
00:04:24.685 --> 00:04:28.666
Mother smiled at them as if she could discern their very thoughts.

50
00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:35.136
But she said kindly: "I just want to say that this meal is a gift from me and Hannah to you.

51
00:04:35.137 --> 00:04:39.105
However you want to use your gift is entirely up to you.

52
00:04:39.106 --> 00:04:43.248
I will love and respect you whatever you decide."

53
00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:51.827
Meg spoke first. "Mother, the girls and I would be honored if the Hummels could enjoy this lovely meal."

54
00:04:51.828 --> 00:04:59.178
Jo and Beth nodded in agreement. A moment or two later, Amy nodded too.

55
00:04:59.179 --> 00:05:03.585
"My girls, I am so proud of you," Mother said.

56
00:05:03.586 --> 00:05:08.020
"Let's all go together to visit the Hummels," suggested Beth.

57
00:05:08.021 --> 00:05:12.052
So the girls sprinted upstairs to change their clothes.

58
00:05:12.053 --> 00:05:16.289
Within a few minutes, the food was all wrapped up and ready to go.

59
00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:20.493
The girls got into their boots and coats and ventured out.

60
00:05:20.494 --> 00:05:23.876
Each of them carried large baskets filled with food.

61
00:05:23.877 --> 00:05:29.094
As the Hummels did not have any heating, Jo hauled a sack of wood as well.

62
00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:32.723
None of the girls felt regret or resentment.

63
00:05:32.724 --> 00:05:37.978
Deep in their hearts, they knew the Hummels would relish the meal much more than they would.

64
00:05:37.979 --> 00:05:43.000
As they passed the old mansion next to their house, Jo happened to look up.

65
00:05:43.001 --> 00:05:48.618
From the third floor, a dark-haired boy peered down at them as they trudged along.

66
00:05:48.619 --> 00:05:54.221
"Look! There's old Mr. Laurence's grandson!" Jo called out to her sisters.

67
00:05:54.222 --> 00:05:58.308
"Jo!" reprimanded Meg. "Stop staring at him.

68
00:05:58.309 --> 00:06:02.729
It isn't proper for a young girl to stare at a boy!"

69
00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:06.722
"Don't be such a granny, Meg," snorted Jo.

70
00:06:06.723 --> 00:06:13.205
Since both her hands were full, she lifted up her foot and wiggled it at him as an alternative to waving.

71
00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:17.753
"Jo! You're so shameless!" said Amy in rebuke.

72
00:06:17.754 --> 00:06:22.412
From the window the boy also lifted his foot and wiggled it at Jo.

73
00:06:22.413 --> 00:06:25.807
Jo let out a loud, hearty laugh.

74
00:06:25.808 --> 00:06:31.511
No words could describe how grateful the Hummel family was for the generous gift.

75
00:06:31.512 --> 00:06:38.040
Jo expertly got a fire going in no time while Meg and Amy set up the table and filled it with food.

76
00:06:38.041 --> 00:06:41.977
Beth and Mother took care of the sick children.

77
00:06:41.978 --> 00:06:50.439
"Did you see how happy those children were?" Amy said, as the girls walked back home, her footsteps light and perky.

78
00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:56.880
"Mrs. Hummel could not stop crying," remarked Jo. "I felt so sorry for her."

79
00:06:56.881 --> 00:07:01.971
"Hopefully Mr. Hummel will be able to return home soon," said Mother.

80
00:07:01.972 --> 00:07:06.147
Silently, all the girls prayed for their father to do the same.

81
00:07:06.148 --> 00:07:10.886
As the girls got nearer to their house, something made them stop.

82
00:07:10.887 --> 00:07:14.101
"Is that our house?" asked Amy.

83
00:07:14.102 --> 00:07:19.192
"Well, I think so, but it looks different somehow," replied Meg.

84
00:07:19.193 --> 00:07:23.755
There was a warm glow to the house as if each room was emitting heat.

85
00:07:23.756 --> 00:07:27.530
"What if the house is on fire?" Jo shouted.

86
00:07:27.531 --> 00:07:33.460
She tore across the field, her hair flying out of its bun, and threw open the door.

87
00:07:33.461 --> 00:07:40.867
What a sight to behold! The entire house was cozily warm, a fire burning brightly in each fireplace.

88
00:07:40.868 --> 00:07:46.492
The bare dining room table was once again crowded with all sorts of delights.

89
00:07:46.493 --> 00:07:51.137
"Hannah! What is this?" Mother demanded to know.

90
00:07:51.138 --> 00:07:57.877
Choking back tears, Hannah could produce no reply but simply pointed to the mansion next door.

91
00:07:57.878 --> 00:08:02.532
"You mean Mr. Laurence sent this?" asked Mother.

92
00:08:02.533 --> 00:08:06.945
Hannah nodded, overcome by a fresh wave of tears.

93
00:08:06.946 --> 00:08:11.474
"Here's a card!" Jo waved a small piece of paper in the air:

94
00:08:11.475 --> 00:08:16.508
Dear Mrs. March and all her lovely daughters, Jo read:

95
00:08:16.509 --> 00:08:24.928
My grandson and I would like to give a gift to you as you so generously give to others. Your neighbor, Mr. Laurence.

96
00:08:24.929 --> 00:08:31.930
The girls all grabbed hands and started to dance around the table. Never had they been so surprised.

97
00:08:31.931 --> 00:08:44.101
"You see, girls," Mother said happily. "When you think of others, others are also thinking of you."

